{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/1162","id":1213373895,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz885IUp3H","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/1162","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/1162.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/1162.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/1162","number":1162,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Align behaviour of dns_config.restricted_nameservers to tailscale","user":{"login":"dbevacqua","id":6534306,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MzQzMDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6534306?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbevacqua","html_url":"https://github.com/dbevacqua","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbevacqua/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbevacqua/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbevacqua/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbevacqua/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbevacqua/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbevacqua/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbevacqua/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbevacqua/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dbevacqua/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #1161 \r\n\r\nTailscale allows split DNS configuration without requiring global nameservers.\r\n\r\nIn addition, as per [the docs](https://tailscale.com/kb/1054/dns/#using-dns-settings-in-the-admin-console):\r\n\r\n> These nameservers also configure search domains for your devices\r\n\r\n~In addition, as stated in [the FAQ](https://tailscale.com/kb/1054/dns/#faq):~\r\n\r\n> ~Previous versions of the DNS settings page allowed defining search domains separately from nameservers. However, due to cross-platform compatibility reasons, this is no longer possible. To define a search domain, you’ll need to add at least one nameserver along with it.~\r\n\r\nThis commit aligns headscale to tailscale by:\r\n\r\n * ~removing support for `dns_config.domains`~\r\n * honouring `dns_config.restricted_nameservers` regardless of whether any global resolvers are configured\r\n * adding a search domain for each nameserver in `restricted_nameservers`\r\n\r\n~I realise \"removing support for dns_config.domains\" may be controversial as the tailscale client still supports search domains being defined separately, though it seems likely that this \"undocumented\" behaviour could (/should) be removed in future. Happy to adjust the change if required.~\r\n\r\nEDIT: removed \"removing support for dns_config.domains\" as it is a breaking change.\r\n\r\nIf the changes look good, I'll update changelog etc.\r\n\r\n<!-- Please tick if the following things apply. You… -->\r\n\r\n- [x] read the [CONTRIBUTING guidelines](README.md#contributing)\r\n- [x] raised a GitHub issue or discussed it on the projects chat beforehand\r\n- [ ] added unit tests\r\n- [ ] added integration tests\r\n- [x] updated documentation if needed\r\n- [ ] updated CHANGELOG.md\r\n\r\n<!-- If applicable, please reference the issue using `Fixes #XXX` and add tests to cover your new code. -->\r\n","created_at":"2023-01-23T12:30:49Z","updated_at":"2023-01-30T23:15:49Z","closed_at":"2023-01-30T23:15:49Z","merged_at":"2023-01-30T23:15:49Z","merge_commit_sha":"385fd93e73aaade882a6a3bffec3478bffe9aa66","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradal